course: dictionary
lesson: 9577
title: Stratosphere: high up in the air
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The stratosphere is a layer of air high above the ground. The air around us is called the atmosphere, and it sits in layers, one above the other. «Higher up, in the stratosphere, there is a layer of a gas called ozone.» The words «higher up» are a clue: the stratosphere is above the layer where we live and where weather happens.
explain: Scientists say the stratosphere is roughly between ten and fifty kilometres above the ground. That is far higher than any hill, and higher than the big planes fly. «The ozone layer in the stratosphere soaks up much of the Sun's harmful ultraviolet light.» So the stratosphere protects us, even though we never go there.
explain: Stratosphere can also be used in a looser way, in everyday talk. «Prices went into the stratosphere» does not mean prices flew up into the air. It means they rose very, very high. Ask yourself: does the sentence make sense if I swap in very high? If it does, you have found the meaning.
fact: The stratosphere is a layer of the atmosphere, the air around the Earth.
fact: The stratosphere is roughly between ten and fifty kilometres above the ground.
fact: The ozone layer is found in the stratosphere, and it soaks up much of the Sun's harmful ultraviolet light.
fact: Big planes fly near the bottom of the atmosphere, below the stratosphere.
fact: In everyday talk, «prices went into the stratosphere» means prices rose very high.
exercise: «The ozone layer in the stratosphere soaks up much of the Sun's harmful ultraviolet light.» What is the stratosphere? | A deep hole under the sea | *A layer of air high above the ground | The top of a tall mountain | A fast kind of train
exercise: Copy the word from «Higher up, in the stratosphere, there is a layer of a gas called ozone» that names the gas. | Sun | layer | stratosphere | *ozone
exercise: «Prices went into the stratosphere.» What does this mean? | *They rose very high | They stayed exactly the same | They fell all the way to the ground | They were hidden in the air
test: In science, which layer of the atmosphere is the one where weather happens? | Stratosphere | Mesosphere | *Troposphere | Ozone layer
test: Where do big planes fly, compared with the stratosphere? | *Near the bottom of the atmosphere, below the stratosphere | Far above the stratosphere, in space | Under the ground | Inside the ozone layer
exam: Which sentence uses stratosphere in the informal way, to mean a very high level? | «Big planes fly near the bottom of the atmosphere.» | *«Prices went into the stratosphere.» | «The ozone layer is in the stratosphere.»
